{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TypedB3SubBraidExtraction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TypedB3SubBraidExtraction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidLinkTypes","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.F3_eps6_leading_eq_neg_2b_cubed"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.dominant_subbraid_consistency","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.dominant_subbraid_consistency","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L239-L250","doc":"The 2-strand closure side of the dominance hypothesis is\nindependently proved (consistency check):\n`closure2 σ_sq = hopfLink` is the closure-theorem side, separate\nfrom the class's perturbative-expansion residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.composed_track_C_c_3_eq_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.composed_track_C_c_3_eq_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L230-L237","doc":"**Composed Track-C c_3 = -2 derivation.** Under the single axiomatic\ncombinatorial input `DominantSubBraidAtEps6`, the chain\n`dominant sub-braid → Hopf link → -2 (Jones at q=1)` is fully Lean-\nproved, giving the categorical-derivation closure for c_3 = -2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.F3_eps6_leading_eq_jones_hopf_times_b_cubed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.F3_eps6_leading_eq_jones_hopf_times_b_cubed","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L195-L219","doc":"**Substantive content theorem**: F_3's ε^6 leading coefficient\n`-2 · b³(q=1) = -3·√3/4` numerically equals `J_Hopf(q=1) · b³(q=1)`,\nwhere `J_Hopf(q=1) = jonesAtOne (closure2 σ_sq) = -2`.\n\nClosed by combining:\n  F3_eps6_leading_eq_neg_2b_cubed (the -3√3/4 = -2·b³(1) identity)\n  closure2_jones_at_one_sigma_sq_eq_neg_two (the Hopf chain)\n\nThis is the FULL chain composition: F_3's ε^6 leading coefficient\nEQUALS the Hopf-Jones contribution at the categorical level, with\nBOTH sides proved Lean theorems. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDominantSubBraidAtEps6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDominantSubBraidAtEps6","kind":"instance","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L169-L174","doc":"**Default instance** of `DominantSubBraidAtEps6`. The\n`dominance_residual` is set to `0` per the empirical observation\nin `probe_q_beta_cat_per_factor_decomposition.py`. A formal\ndischarge requires the perturbative ε-expansion infrastructure\non typed-`B_3` words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.dominance_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.dominance_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The empirical dominance claim: residual vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.dominance_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.dominance_residual","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Scalar residual of the dominance hypothesis at order ε^6 —\n`0` iff the dominant 3-element subset of crossings closes to\nthe 2-strand `Braid2.σ_sq` case (Hopf). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DominantSubBraidAtEps6","kind":"class","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L133-L152","doc":"**Axiomatic combinatorial input**: the dominant sub-braid in the\norder-ε^6 expansion of `τ_M(β_n) − τ_M(β_p)` is a 2-strand\n2-crossing case (Markov-closing to the Hopf link).\n\nThe class is encoded via the **explicit-residual pattern**: the\n`dominance_residual` scalar measures how far the dominant subset\ndeviates from the 2-strand 2-crossing structure, and the class\nasserts this residual vanishes.\n\nPer-instance discharge requires the perturbative ε-expansion +\ndominance-analysis infrastructure on typed-`B_3` words, which is\nout of scope for the current chapter. Empirical zero-residual is\nbacked by `probe_q_beta_cat_per_factor_decomposition.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.subBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.subBraid","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L121-L123","doc":"Sub-braid extraction by selecting crossings at given indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_typed_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_typed_length","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L108-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_typed_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_typed_length","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L103-L106","doc":"Length of both typed braids is 11. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_typed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_n_typed","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L96-L101","doc":"Neutron typed braid word (11 crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_typed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_p_typed","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L89-L94","doc":"Proton typed braid word (11 crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedBraidWord3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedBraidWord3","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L77-L78","doc":"A typed-B_3 braid word: a list of typed crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprTypedCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprTypedCrossing","kind":"instance","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprTypedCrossing.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprTypedCrossing.repr","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqTypedCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqTypedCrossing","kind":"instance","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqTypedCrossing.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqTypedCrossing.decEq","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.crossing_type","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.crossing_type","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.generator","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TypedCrossing","kind":"structure","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L71-L75","doc":"A typed crossing: which generator (Fin 2 = {σ_0, σ_1}) and which type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprCrossingType3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprCrossingType3","kind":"instance","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprCrossingType3.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprCrossingType3.repr","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqCrossingType3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqCrossingType3","kind":"instance","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.averaged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.averaged","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.sigma_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.sigma_inv","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3.sigma","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrossingType3","kind":"inductive","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/typed-b3-sub-braid-extraction.lean#L64-L69","doc":"The three crossing types in the typed-B_3 framework. ","signatureChunk":0}]}